    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; the other two files are a base class and a helper).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature end-to-end, following the existing derived-field pattern (like `displayName`/`initials`) used throughout this Spring Boot app.\n\n**API contract** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`):\n- Added an optional `title` input field to `OwnerFields`, constrained to the enum `MR`/`MRS`/`MS`/`DR`.\n- Added a read-only `salutation` output field to `Owner`.\n\n**Domain model** (`model/Owner.java`):\n- Added a persisted `title` column with getter/setter.\n- Added `getSalutation()`: returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when the title is null/empty.\n\n**Mapping** (`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`):\n- Added an `@AfterMapping` method to fill `salutation` from `Owner.getSalutation()`. MapStruct auto-maps the `title` enum\u2194`String` (verified in the generated `OwnerMapperImpl`: stored as `enum.name()`, read back via `valueOf`).\n\n**Controller** (`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- Propagated `title` in the manual field-copy of `updateOwner` for consistency.\n\n**Persistence** \u2014 added the `title` column to all four schema variants (`hsqldb` \u2014 used by tests, plus `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (posts `title=DR`, `lastName=who`, expects `salutation=\"DR who\"`) and the full suite pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
