    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is coherent, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase.\n\n- **Domain logic placement is correct and consistent.** `Owner` already hosts a family of domain-computed, derived getters over stored fields \u2014 `getTelephoneDisplay()`, `getAgeBand()`, `getCheckDigit()`, `getMembershipNumber()`, `getMembershipLevel()`. `getSalutation()` (combining the newly-stored `title` field with `lastName`, with null/empty handling) fits that established pattern exactly. Since `title` is a real persisted field, deriving the salutation on the entity is the natural home.\n- **The mapper delegation matches the dominant local idiom.** `addSalutation` is a thin `@AfterMapping` that copies from the domain getter \u2014 identical in shape to `addCheckDigit`, `addMembershipNumber`, `addMembershipLevel`, and `addAgeBand`. It correctly does *not* imitate the two trivial inline formatters (`addDisplayName`, `addInitials`), which is the right call given salutation carries real branching logic.\n- **No duplication or catch-all growth.** The formatting rule lives in one place; the mapper doesn't re-implement it. Field, getter/setter, and schema/OpenAPI additions are placed conventionally alongside their peers.\n- **Controller wiring is reasonable.** The `getValue()` null-guard is the standard way to unwrap the generated enum DTO into the entity's `String` field.\n\nA maintainer of this repo would find all of this natural and in-keeping.",
